Cobi fork patch 0007: an app-set proxy for libVLC's http/https modules.

Why: iOS, tvOS and Mac Catalyst have no system proxy setting that
vlc_getProxyUrl() could read. Cobi Player routes only its own traffic through
the user's VPN or proxy via an in-process gateway on 127.0.0.1, so the app
hands libVLC the gateway's address with vlc_darwin_SetProxyUrl(). While it is
set, every http and https connection goes to it; there is no direct fallback.

The gateway gets a fresh login on every start ("http://user:pass@127.0.0.1:port")
so that no other local process can use it. libVLC already sent that login on
CONNECT (https, tunnel.c) and in the legacy http.c module, but not on plain-http
requests of the http module (connmgr.c -> vlc_h1_request, absolute-form), which
is also the path HLS/DASH segments take. connmgr.c now adds the same Basic
Proxy-Authorization to every request that goes to the proxy, reused
connections included.

Files: include/vlc_network.h (declaration), src/darwin/netconf.m (the app
proxy), modules/access/http/connmgr.c (login on plain http).
Not upstream; the 0007 number is this fork's own sequence.

